{"Browser reporting validation changes API response shape and status codes (now returns 422 with JSON error details), potentially breaking downstream callers": 0.5034684538841248, "Detector.update() reads wrong key 'detector_type' instead of serializer field 'type', causing validated data to be ignored and potential AttributeError if instance.group_type is already a slug string": 0.29416623711586, "TypedDict ErrorEvent is used like a constructor (ErrorEvent(...)) which will raise TypeError at runtime since TypedDict is not callable": 0.7695165872573853, "Feature-flagged TableWidgetVisualization renders with hard-coded empty arrays/objects for columns, data, and meta instead of actual result data, showing blank tables to users": 0.9933034777641296, "BrowserReportSerializer allows both 'age' and 'timestamp' to be optional without enforcing that at least one is present, potentially violating spec requirements": 0.6876787543296814, "make_seer_request logs full response.text and response.content on failure, potentially exposing sensitive information or PII in application logs": 0.12601616978645325, "TabularColumn.name is typed as TFields (same as key) instead of plain string, conflating semantic roles and preventing arbitrary display strings": 0.34105032682418823, "Header alignment in renderDefaultHeadCell uses column.name instead of column.key for fieldAlignment, causing incorrect alignment when display names differ from field keys": 0.6989213824272156, "Object.keys(tableData?.meta.fields) can raise TypeError if tableData or meta is undefined due to incomplete optional chaining": 0.8978286385536194, "BrowserReportingCollector logs raw request.data and serializer.errors which may contain PII or sensitive information": 0.6535463929176331}